{"_id":"68a736208ec3d8323af18c84","nodeId":"XOXsjaQ-YyuAMpVCqH8KG","roadmapSlug":"ios","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:12.170Z","description":"# MapKit\n\nMapKit is Apple's framework for embedding maps and location-based features into iOS apps. It provides interactive map views, annotation pins, overlays, turn-by-turn directions, and local place search. MapKit uses Apple Maps as its data source and integrates with Core Location for GPS access.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"MapKit","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/mapkit/","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf86b8"},{"type":"article","title":"Implement MapKit APIs","url":"https://medium.com/simform-engineering/mapkit-swiftui-in-ios-17-1fec82c3bf00","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf86b9"},{"type":"video","title":"Meet MapKit for SwiftUI","url":"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2023/10043/","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf86ba"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:04:24.838Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/ios/content/XOXsjaQ-YyuAMpVCqH8KG.md"}